  <h1>AI Alignment, Observation Fibers &amp; Safe Action Under Uncertainty</h1>
  <p class="lead">Population-marginal RLHF collapses missing user context into a median prior and keys safety on surface lexical tokens. Hyperactivity replaces both with exact observation-fiber inference: keep underdetermination explicit as \(\mathsf{Fib}_o(y)\), act only when \(\mathsf{SafeAt}(y)\) is inhabited across every compatible world, and query to shrink the fiber when it is not.</p>
  <div class="pill-row">
    <a class="pill" href="/alignment-is-standpoint">Paper: Alignment Is Standpoint</a>
    <a class="pill" href="/training-agents-into-weights">Note: Training Agents Into Weights</a>
    <a class="pill" href="/neuro">Neuro Co-Processor Lab</a>
    <a class="pill" href="/paper#part-i">Part I §1 &amp; §10.4</a>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>1. Interactive Fiber Safety &amp; Active Querying (InterACT / §10.4)</h2>
      <span class="mod-tag">lib/observation.cub · neuro/coproc.cub · chem/basin-compose.cub</span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <span>Compatible World Fiber Fib_o(y)</span>
          <span id="aiBadge" class="badge bad">SafeAt(y) UNINHABITED · MUST QUERY</span>
        </div>
        <div class="worlds" id="worldGrid"></div>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <button class="btn primary" id="btnQuery">Issue Clarifying Query (Update K → K')</button>
          <button class="btn" id="btnLex">Apply Surface Lexical Filter Only</button>
          <button class="btn" id="btnReset">Reset Fiber</button>
        </div>
        <p id="aiNote" style="font:500 12px var(--mono);color:var(--muted);margin:12px 0 0">4 candidate worlds compatible with initial prompt. Action is unsafe in 2 of them → SafeAt(y) is empty.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="thm"><b>SafeAt(y) (10.11) &amp; WorldAfter (10.12)</b> — An action is safe at reading \(y\) iff \(\prod_{(s,p):\mathsf{Fib}_o(y)} P(s)\). When a split witness (<code>Disagreement</code>) exists, <code>disagreement-blocks-activation</code> forbids acting and synthesizes the discriminating query to collapse the fiber.</div>
        <p><b>Why lexical safety fails (`no-observed-law`, `lexical-gate-fails`):</b> Click <i>Apply Surface Lexical Filter Only</i>. Because distinct intents share surface tokens, the compatible fiber still contains an unsafe world—so no safety law descends through surface words alone.</p>
        <pre>Warrants : (H → O) → O → (H → Type) → Type
Warrants o y P = (hp : fiber o y) → P (fst hp)
query-establishes-safe : ((w w' : W) → K w → H w r w' → P w')
  → SafeOver (WorldAfter K H r) P</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
